          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;â€œWeaver!â€ Adora screamed over the comms, desperate to get some kind of response, â€œSergeant Weaver! Do you copy?!â€ She paused, hand shaking violently as she clutched onto her radio. She looked at the burning building in flames right in front of her. Tears welled in her eyes and a deep pit of anxiety brewed in her stomach at the lack of response, â€œFuck! Catra, baby, &lt;em&gt;please&lt;/em&gt;!"&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œIâ€™m here,â€ Catra choked out, her voice &lt;em&gt;just&lt;/em&gt; not overshadowed by the crushing sounds of the building collapsing with her still inside, â€œIâ€™m alive.â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-&lt;br /&gt;Captain Adora Grey of the Brightmoon Police Department (BMPD) and her ex-wife Sergeant Catra Weaver respond to  an active shooter scene at their local mall.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
